    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "# H1+H3 outside Hand Cannoneer"
      },
      {
        "id": "executive_summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "sweep_results",
        "body": "## Executive Summary\n\n- **Do not promote H1+H3 globally to every ranged-vs-melee fight.** The median absolute gap improves from **8.65 pp to 7.14 pp**, but the target pass count falls from **18/21 to 16/21** and correct winners fall from **20/21 to 17/21**.\n- **Arbalester clearly benefits.** All seven families land within 25 pp, with mean absolute gap improving from **14.55 pp to 8.13 pp** and no winner regressions.\n- **Heavy Cavalry Archer is mixed.** Mean gap worsens slightly from **13.27 pp to 14.60 pp**, and Halberdier changes from the correct melee winner to the wrong ranged winner.\n- **Imperial Elite Skirmisher breaks.** Mean gap rises from **16.63 pp to 47.24 pp**; Champion reverses to the wrong winner, and every Paladin run reaches the 600-second cap."
      },
      {
        "id": "definitions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## What was measured\n\nThe population is every FINAL recording for Arbalester, Heavy Cavalry Archer, and Imperial Elite Skirmisher against the seven standard melee units: **133 recordings in 21 families**. Each arm uses the exact tape spawn for **five deterministic seeds per recording**—665 simulations per arm and 1,330 total. Signed winner HP is positive when the ranged line wins and negative when it loses. Success means the simulated median is within **25 percentage points** of the FINAL family median and has the same winner."
      },
      {
        "id": "broad_pattern",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "sweep_results",
        "body": "## The center improves, but the tail gets much worse\n\nH1+H3 improves 11 families, regresses nine, and leaves one unchanged. That nudges the median gap down, yet three severe failures lift the mean gap from **14.81 pp to 23.32 pp**. The chart shows the effect family by family; positive bars mean the change moved closer to tape."
      },
      {
        "id": "gap_chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "gap_change"
      },
      {
        "id": "line_readout",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "sweep_results",
        "body": "## Arbalester is the reusable part; the other lines need scoping\n\nArbalester improves in six of seven families and gains two threshold passes: Hussar moves from 26.72 pp off to 13.98 pp off, while Paladin improves from 21.67 pp to just 0.76 pp. Heavy Cavalry Archer gains substantially against Champion but loses the tape winner against Halberdier. Elite Skirmisher has two modest improvements, but the large Champion and Paladin failures dominate the line."
      },
      {
        "id": "line_table",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "line_summary"
      },
      {
        "id": "failure_modes",
        "type": "markdown",
        "sourceId": "sweep_results",
        "body": "## Three outcome failures block a global rollout\n\n- **Champion vs Imperial Elite Skirmisher:** FINAL and base both have Champion winning near 54% HP; H1+H3 instead gives the skirmisher the win at 71.43% HP in all 20 runs.\n- **Paladin vs Imperial Elite Skirmisher:** FINAL is Paladin +87.46% and base is Paladin +90.24%; all 20 H1+H3 runs hit the 600-second cap.\n- **Halberdier vs Heavy Cavalry Archer:** FINAL is Halberdier +16.27% and base is Halberdier +24.92%; H1+H3 flips all 50 runs to Heavy Cavalry Archer +30.69%.\n\nThese are deterministic family-wide changes in this sweep, not isolated seed noise."
      },
      {
        "id": "detail_table",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "matchup_detail"
      },
      {
        "id": "next_steps",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Recommended next steps\n\n1. Keep H1+H3 enabled for Hand Cannoneer while it remains experimental.\n2. Test a line-scoped Arbalester version; its seven-family result is strong enough to justify an isolated gate.\n3. Do not enable H3 obstacle steering for Imperial Elite Skirmisher until its low-speed escape behavior and Paladin cap are understood.\n4. Diagnose the Heavy Cavalry Archer–Halberdier reversal before considering that line."
      },
      {
        "id": "questions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Further questions\n\n- Is the reusable mechanism the H1 post-swing plant, the H3 clockwise obstacle steering, or their interaction?\n- Should H3 require a minimum ranged-unit speed or a Hand Cannoneer/Arbalester-specific behavior state?\n- Does the Imperial Elite Skirmisher cap come from a stable orbit that Paladins cannot close, or from target/path deadlock?"
      },
      {
        "id": "caveats",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Caveats and assumptions\n\nOnly the locked FINAL archive was used (SHA-256 `31A31FE39C025DDD88EB1F502FD62E0EC48464F4CBB72C1693D5C4FEED0713C9`). Family medians combine every FINAL recording and five simulation seeds per recording. Fight duration is not an optimization target; it is mentioned only where a run never resolves, because a capped run has no valid winner-HP outcome. H1+H3 remains an isolated calibration branch, not production behavior."
      }
    ]
  },
